    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. All tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted every rejection handler that was still emitting a plain `Map.of(\"errors\", \u2026)` body over to RFC7807 `application/problem+json`, using the existing `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper already used by the validation/500/403 handlers. That helper populates all four required members \u2014 `type` (`about:blank`), `title` (exception simple name), `status` (via `ProblemDetail.forStatus`), and `detail` \u2014 and OfficeFloor serializes `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` as `application/problem+json`.\n\nHandlers updated (HTTP status codes unchanged):\n\n- **400** \u2014 `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler`, `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler`, `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`, `DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler`, `FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`, `MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler` (its field list is preserved as a `fields` problem property)\n- **409** \u2014 `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler`, `CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`\n- **429** \u2014 `DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler`\n\nThe `MethodArgumentNotValidException` path was already problem+json, so I left it as is.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
